Host-side tests for Core OpenGL (CGL)
=====================================

The CGL implementation in Frameworks/OpenGL is plain C plus pthreads and
does not depend on a GPU, so it is tested on the build host:

    make -C Frameworks/OpenGL/tests          (GNU make or bmake)

clang is used by default, as in the Minkar build; pass CC=... to
override. Until the desktop GL headers replace the GLES2 ones, gcc
rejects their #import directives under -Werror.

This builds the CGL sources together with each test under
AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer and runs:

  test_cgl          The CGL API against a recording test driver:
                    argument validation, pixel formats, renderer info,
                    contexts and share groups, parameters, enables, the
                    per-thread current context, off-screen drawables,
                    pixel buffers and global options.

  test_null_driver  The built-in null renderer, with and without
                    CGL_ENABLE_NULL_RENDERER=1.

  test_gl_dispatch  The exported gl* entry points: forwarding to the
                    current context's driver (float/double arguments,
                    return values), per-thread contexts, and no-ops
                    without a context or driver function.

Add a test here whenever CGL behavior changes or a new driver callback
is added.
